qemu: pflash_cfi01: don't skip buffered-write start when word count is 0

The CFI buffered-write count is N-1 encoded, so a count of 0 is a valid
single-word write (Linux's Intel CFI driver emits it for single bus-word
chunks). The "&& pfl->counter" gate never opens the update buffer for it,
the write is rejected, and UBI on vexpress-qemu-flash switches to read-only
mode.

https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu/-/issues/4111

--- a/hw/block/pflash_cfi01.c
+++ b/hw/block/pflash_cfi01.c
@@ -597,9 +597,9 @@
     case 2:
         switch (pfl->cmd) {
         case 0xe8: /* Block write */
             /* FIXME check @offset, @width */
-            if (pfl->blk_offset == -1 && pfl->counter) {
+            if (pfl->blk_offset == -1) {
                 pflash_blk_write_start(pfl, offset);
             }
             if (!pfl->ro && (pfl->blk_offset != -1)) {
                 pflash_data_write(pfl, offset, value, width, be);
